From 1ae84adb938de476d47aa13f1d1343d300f7fcc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:29:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] f_decoder_wrapper: prefer bitstream stereo 3D layout
 over container tag
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

fix_image_params() unconditionally overwrote the layout with the
container tag, so the value mp_image_from_av_frame() reads from
AV_FRAME_DATA_STEREO3D never reached the output. Fall back to the tag
only when the bitstream signals nothing, the same rule rotation already
follows.

Fixes: #18489
Co-authored-by: Kacper Michajłow <kasper93@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit a860bc42bae5b4aa08880dc7efefed955931ae41)
---
 filters/f_decoder_wrapper.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/filters/f_decoder_wrapper.c b/filters/f_decoder_wrapper.c
index 5e2e8d74c0..037bdb531e 100644
--- a/filters/f_decoder_wrapper.c
+++ b/filters/f_decoder_wrapper.c
@@ -610,7 +610,8 @@ static void fix_image_params(struct priv *p,
     if (m.p_w <= 0 || m.p_h <= 0)
         m.p_w = m.p_h = 1;
 
-    m.stereo3d = p->codec->stereo_mode;
+    if (!m.stereo3d)
+        m.stereo3d = p->codec->stereo_mode;
 
     if (!mp_rect_equals(&p->codec->crop, &(struct mp_rect){0})) {
         struct mp_rect crop = p->codec->crop;
